  <figcaption class="mb-6 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="mb-2 text-sm font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] text-primary uppercase">
      Control boundary
    </p>
    <h3
      id="trust-architecture-title"
      class="text-2xl font-bold text-card-foreground sm:text-3xl"
    >
      One bounded path from request to record
    </h3>
    <p
      id="trust-architecture-description"
      class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground sm:text-base"
    >
      Hyper Tern routes an approved request, Hyper-ABS limits exposed context,
      and Hyper-0x records the resulting execution event. Each layer depends on
      the surrounding deployment and policy configuration.
    </p>
  </figcaption>

  <div
    class="overflow-x-auto pb-2"
    tabindex="0"
    aria-label="Scrollable trust architecture diagram"
  >
    <svg
      class="h-auto min-w-[760px]"
      viewBox="0 0 1120 470"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="trust-svg-title trust-svg-description"
    >
      <title id="trust-svg-title">Buckleson trust and execution architecture</title>
      <desc id="trust-svg-description">
        An AI request passes through Hyper Tern and Hyper-ABS to an AI model and
        an application. Hyper-0x records the execution event for later
        verification.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <marker
          id="trust-arrow"
          viewBox="0 0 10 10"
          refX="8"
          refY="5"
          markerWidth="7"
          markerHeight="7"
